ade object to fly past Uranus, Voyager 2's short-range observations\",\"corrects\":\"Voyager 1's short-range observations\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"Voyager 2 is the only Uranus flyby spacecraft.\"},{\"statement\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED Jan. 24, 1986, at a range of about 81,500 kilometers (50,640 miles).\",\"corrects\":\"Jan. 24, 1968, at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles)\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"Encounter was 1986; 81,500 km is 50,640 mi, units were swapped.\"},{\"statement\":\"during their space shuttle launch Jan. 28, 1986.\",\"corrects\":\"launch Feb. 28, 1986\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"Challenger launched and was lost on Jan. 28, 1986.\"}]}","ttft_ms":13867,"type":"result","duration_ms":25143,"uuid":"848000b0-1238-43f6-8589-bb2bea72fc15","ttft_stream_ms":1174,"time_to_request_ms":101,"first_content_frame_ms":1174,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
